<!--
  The mark the name borrows from is a light O with a darker letter laid over it, and two things
  make that a mark rather than two letters. The O's counter is 0.29 of its outer radius, far tighter
  than any typeface draws one. And the second letter sits *over* the O in the deeper of the two
  blues, so the overlap goes dark instead of knocking out. Both are kept here, with an S standing in
  for the other letter, because the name is the joke and the icon may as well be.

  So the O is geometry, not type: an evenOdd donut, radius 19.5 with a 5.66 counter, centred on
  44.29,54. The S is Archivo Black, extracted from the .ttf as outlines and left upright — the mark
  it is standing in for leans, but a leaning S reads as an italic rather than as a logo, so it does
  not lean here. The path below is the plain glyph and re-extracting it from the .ttf is enough.

  What sets the S's position is the counter: it is scaled to the O's full height and set 3.7 right
  of the O's centre, which is where its spine stops closing on the hole. Measured by rendering it,
  not by eye — the same render puts the pair's furthest point 30.6 out from its centre at 54,54,
  inside the 33 the adaptive-icon safe zone allows.
-->
